# XSH sigwait()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.sigwait.001
anchor     functions/sigwait.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       With SIGUSR1 and SIGUSR2 blocked and pending, sigwait() on a set
           holding only SIGUSR1 returns 0 with *sig set to SIGUSR1; SIGUSR1
           is no longer pending, SIGUSR2 still is, and no handler runs.
uses       XSH.sigpending.001
test       t/001-takes-pending.c

assertion  XSH.sigwait.002
anchor     functions/sigwait.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       With nothing pending, sigwait() returns only after a signal in the
           set, sent 300 ms later, becomes pending.
test       t/002-waits.c

assertion  XSH.sigwait.003
anchor     functions/sigwait.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       With two occurrences of SIGRTMIN queued by sigqueue() (SA_SIGINFO
           set), sigwait() takes one and the other is still pending.
uses       XSH.sigqueue.001 XSH.sigpending.001
test       t/003-queued-remain.c

assertion  XSH.sigwait.004
anchor     functions/sigwait.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       With SIGRTMIN+2 and then SIGRTMIN+1 pending, sigwait() on both
           returns SIGRTMIN+1 first.
test       t/004-lowest-rt.c

assertion  XSH.sigwait.005
anchor     functions/sigwait.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       With two threads in sigwait() for SIGUSR1, pthread_kill() to the
           second makes it return with SIGUSR1 (within 2 s), and the first
           goes on waiting.
test       t/005-thread-directed.c

assertion  XSH.sigwait.006
anchor     functions/sigwait.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       With two threads in sigwait() for SIGUSR1, one SIGUSR1 sent to the
           process returns exactly one of them.
test       t/006-one-waiter.c
